A.qo=s(["Every figure here is arithmetic over the counter readings and rupee amounts YOU typed in. ginlekha ships no reference data of any kind \u2014 no cartridge yields, no cost-per-page norms, no machine specifications.","It does not interpolate. Pages are counted only between two readings you actually took. A month with no reading is shown as a gap, not as an estimate.","Rupees dated before your first reading, after your last reading, or inside a stretch ginlekha could not measure (a meter reset) are excluded from every per-page figure and listed separately. Rupees inside a long gap ARE counted \u2014 the pages either side of them were counted too; what ginlekha refuses is to split that gap by month.",'Every per-page figure names its own numerator and denominator. "Running cost per page" excludes the machine\u2019s purchase price; "all-in cost per page" includes it. They are different numbers, always shown together, and one is never quoted as the other.',"ginlekha does not tell you whether to replace, repair or keep the machine, and makes no forecast. A rising recent cost per page has many causes \u2014 a heavy job, a one-off drum, a quiet season, a price rise \u2014 and this app cannot tell them apart.","Cartridge yields are measured between YOUR toner-change readings. A cartridge that was already in the machine when you got it, or that is still running now, is labelled as such and is not a yield.",u.C,'These are MACHINE costs \u2014 only the rupees you entered against this machine. Electricity, rent and your own time are never in them, and paper is in them only if you logged paper invoices; the line beside the figures says which. Elsewhere in the trade "cost per page" usually means paper included, so a page you sell costs more than the figures here.'],t.s)
